[{:db/id "q-95077/selection/742351170426e6325682c570b571670bb9ec49b68650c585cbc48233367542a8" :answer/id #uuid "07e3a6ec-c444-58b0-bbc1-a77c7808b998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95077/selection/866c79191510264e723d38efdd968fe957eb7f813fc1c0e6cf5d5373ed1a5806" :answer/id #uuid "14f4390a-b1b7-58be-b6bc-2f194fe929f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2+t}{\\sqrt{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95077/selection/eb54f30823e7ff5c2256a76e79422603f75b397979bf0c4d3648a2dad8ac8439" :answer/id #uuid "209ebcac-566e-5432-bdb2-d289f670570f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95077/selection/698803eff4dc0214cf3d8dbb8233951cb3abc1fa22e5515a3dff85f5df8abf54" :answer/id #uuid "0b525555-2294-5fac-862b-8f034e0b965e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95077/selection/371599fb232746f698ee5a4ed88ed8ed3e4e87d5febec98791b6a3139a08fd71" :answer/id #uuid "a6fef166-10f9-5474-92b2-95e41ffc57ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95077/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ff04657-66f3-5544-b457-5fe6a6fc531d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95077/selection/698803eff4dc0214cf3d8dbb8233951cb3abc1fa22e5515a3dff85f5df8abf54" :answer-field/choices ["q-95077/selection/742351170426e6325682c570b571670bb9ec49b68650c585cbc48233367542a8" "q-95077/selection/866c79191510264e723d38efdd968fe957eb7f813fc1c0e6cf5d5373ed1a5806" "q-95077/selection/eb54f30823e7ff5c2256a76e79422603f75b397979bf0c4d3648a2dad8ac8439" "q-95077/selection/698803eff4dc0214cf3d8dbb8233951cb3abc1fa22e5515a3dff85f5df8abf54" "q-95077/selection/371599fb232746f698ee5a4ed88ed8ed3e4e87d5febec98791b6a3139a08fd71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95077" :question/id #uuid "15ce73ae-4ec6-57f1-8eb8-09cb1e9834a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-95077" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2xy},x=t$ and $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{2xy}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2xy}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}\\cdot 1+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95077/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ed13b87-51ab-547d-a9ed-960eda7db24e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95077"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-95078"] :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2}),x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$ for $0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x{y}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{2xy}{x{y}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-95076/selection/4eade4cfd3084f6cfca3db64b7d344954ecb2d75a8eafa0628b2ff907ea4413e" :answer/id #uuid "3c1eb904-2a59-5783-9b33-9c1ee939b99f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t(1+2t){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95076/selection/18b4f8201bb49c80aaa87722a4d99eec50d354788ba824ec69b1e0fdb20606f7" :answer/id #uuid "5fa0473f-0977-53d1-b62e-b727f3b35f35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{t}^{3}(2+t){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95076/selection/e13d4a9b95c30912914d9aca783a22d4a66487500070321f37d169d2246d1bf1" :answer/id #uuid "7877f923-de87-546f-976a-91e140e3cf2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8t(1+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95076/selection/252d74cc69d8d5e1f514e0b63ddaf9c3554f402ca892e8bf2f2e2cca508e58f9" :answer/id #uuid "d6d64222-0cf4-5805-9e31-6e26aa99f2ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}(1+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95076/selection/5c5dfec6e42c2359d5351ec0da64d79d0d246e8648d1076503f86bc0bd6466fa" :answer/id #uuid "e9da65c1-cb76-5ead-9fa2-b7819f929374" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t(2+t){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95076/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2afa4a24-5be3-5abc-a8b4-4cd2a74a579b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95076/selection/e13d4a9b95c30912914d9aca783a22d4a66487500070321f37d169d2246d1bf1" :answer-field/choices ["q-95076/selection/4eade4cfd3084f6cfca3db64b7d344954ecb2d75a8eafa0628b2ff907ea4413e" "q-95076/selection/18b4f8201bb49c80aaa87722a4d99eec50d354788ba824ec69b1e0fdb20606f7" "q-95076/selection/e13d4a9b95c30912914d9aca783a22d4a66487500070321f37d169d2246d1bf1" "q-95076/selection/252d74cc69d8d5e1f514e0b63ddaf9c3554f402ca892e8bf2f2e2cca508e58f9" "q-95076/selection/5c5dfec6e42c2359d5351ec0da64d79d0d246e8648d1076503f86bc0bd6466fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95076" :question/id #uuid "d7005bf6-3723-544e-bddf-addae8b8b624" :question/math-academy-id "q-95076" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y},x=2t$ and $y={t}^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(2t){e}^{{t}^{2}}=4t{e}^{{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(2t)^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}=4{t}^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =4t{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2+4{t}^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =8t{e}^{{t}^{2}}+8{t}^{3}{e}^{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =8t(1+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95076/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ed13b87-51ab-547d-a9ed-960eda7db24e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95084/selection/dc381220304be7c72ccb07d995da9b6309e63fba629c353021db062fe8f902b4" :answer/id #uuid "7a87e8e4-ced1-5b8f-89d5-4804d4e56929" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡2s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95084/selection/2e734d2779e4539d1b012e6db29b265b211e39d7a04447f3233c4a4e816dd354" :answer/id #uuid "ca1bdaf6-5fbd-5ebd-8385-88367c25d304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s+{csc}^{2}⁡2s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95084/selection/95a8e8a602b0f9d59801ce7a932120dbf3cd099b835cfd9a791f0a7723ede6c2" :answer/id #uuid "ade39907-996f-5f76-b1d9-298e6d3b4f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}⁡2s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95084/selection/d1d71a3b6e686e48b57261bd1cea720a606b5e0973f483c0fc05da9257293666" :answer/id #uuid "8d879a89-1789-53e5-be9a-50cdc59af0d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95084/selection/6d0c27aa654450d07a09769dfbf1870b733362b4e4da181e9c75c619901ac508" :answer/id #uuid "6251e754-9fc0-5e9b-9fbc-1d45bbbd5cd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95084/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebcd6dbb-dde2-5e3e-b7e9-76d3d882377d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95084/selection/6d0c27aa654450d07a09769dfbf1870b733362b4e4da181e9c75c619901ac508" :answer-field/choices ["q-95084/selection/dc381220304be7c72ccb07d995da9b6309e63fba629c353021db062fe8f902b4" "q-95084/selection/2e734d2779e4539d1b012e6db29b265b211e39d7a04447f3233c4a4e816dd354" "q-95084/selection/95a8e8a602b0f9d59801ce7a932120dbf3cd099b835cfd9a791f0a7723ede6c2" "q-95084/selection/d1d71a3b6e686e48b57261bd1cea720a606b5e0973f483c0fc05da9257293666" "q-95084/selection/6d0c27aa654450d07a09769dfbf1870b733362b4e4da181e9c75c619901ac508"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95084" :question/id #uuid "8a712ea0-8d4b-5b2f-8c02-2dea8af5517a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95084" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y},x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s)+(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s})\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2-2\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s} \\\\  & =-2-2{cot}^{2}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95084/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ed13b87-51ab-547d-a9ed-960eda7db24e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95080/selection/00b0fe7bbe249f08c8a1ae9c0b229fd2f6ad4266ffe27ac46dcd45a2f7ad7db2" :answer/id #uuid "f9efefc5-5732-56f3-8401-04ff1ea25179" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}^{2}{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95080/selection/8a906b39a11b2522842009c5f0ce4b1956d61eb67f82ebffc377766781fda24e" :answer/id #uuid "fef5e5be-3316-5d35-bed3-97686c7c312e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(s+2){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95080/selection/5bf15db36d067875dd75611a46566d69c325bea722b074f1c6e918bd0936b78c" :answer/id #uuid "22a22796-eeb1-55ce-9112-482e06a70bbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s(s+2){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95080/selection/e1047a718a5f7776076ef0b0209116640e4cf1cf6223063213cfb31358cb3a98" :answer/id #uuid "8e5d3846-7c8f-5c52-b905-8f8cdf6e0878" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2s{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95080/selection/e49f3c3808214426ae17ae3895ca82762b2aa62a562063182ee3baadb85ae582" :answer/id #uuid "a059dd82-b692-5cb0-bfef-fcc48e076f49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(s+1){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95080/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "317c888f-9872-5812-a1fa-988130165f61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95080/selection/e49f3c3808214426ae17ae3895ca82762b2aa62a562063182ee3baadb85ae582" :answer-field/choices ["q-95080/selection/00b0fe7bbe249f08c8a1ae9c0b229fd2f6ad4266ffe27ac46dcd45a2f7ad7db2" "q-95080/selection/8a906b39a11b2522842009c5f0ce4b1956d61eb67f82ebffc377766781fda24e" "q-95080/selection/5bf15db36d067875dd75611a46566d69c325bea722b074f1c6e918bd0936b78c" "q-95080/selection/e1047a718a5f7776076ef0b0209116640e4cf1cf6223063213cfb31358cb3a98" "q-95080/selection/e49f3c3808214426ae17ae3895ca82762b2aa62a562063182ee3baadb85ae582"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95080" :question/id #uuid "cb02b03c-1456-5486-9a3f-00df80c414ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-95080" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={e}^{x+2y},x={s}^{2},$ and $y=s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{x+2y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{e}^{x+2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & ={e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}\\cdot 2s+2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2s{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}+2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s} \\\\  & =2(s+1){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95080/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ed13b87-51ab-547d-a9ed-960eda7db24e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95119/selection/d9a7ff0b9c78d589ae01a2defaf54358c6d146f45d82e8dc6872d0b0bdd4295a" :answer/id #uuid "67fe767c-cc16-54c0-867e-856a8153da86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1-2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95119/selection/478f51db7f1628adca5589e28b1b4be95bde8f73ee6c56aca3d493e7ef75d152" :answer/id #uuid "44e00371-c0a7-51cc-b99d-e71453d87614" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1+4{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95119/selection/e517f7b976532162ae0bfcb14575c1cd84f8bea57ba7860d9ed48aef6f66c51c" :answer/id #uuid "eaa3f908-6e8c-5535-bbed-00692e5c9452" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1-4{x}^{3}}{x})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{{x}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95119/selection/1fd73b79f7e3872eb8d68942dbcff463690d27a344ee4a0cc495f332fc142e50" :answer/id #uuid "2186afd0-6435-5dce-aca4-a0e5103dfd15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{x})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95119/selection/44734b7fd9b8fa6db618fbb8bb4edbe1ee576e76d162cea0893b4b9770639b34" :answer/id #uuid "54754aa8-4ebc-5afe-a552-94c94c90c95b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1-3{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95119/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7998fd39-de54-51f7-a96d-5992b98cd6d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95119/selection/d9a7ff0b9c78d589ae01a2defaf54358c6d146f45d82e8dc6872d0b0bdd4295a" :answer-field/choices ["q-95119/selection/d9a7ff0b9c78d589ae01a2defaf54358c6d146f45d82e8dc6872d0b0bdd4295a" "q-95119/selection/478f51db7f1628adca5589e28b1b4be95bde8f73ee6c56aca3d493e7ef75d152" "q-95119/selection/e517f7b976532162ae0bfcb14575c1cd84f8bea57ba7860d9ed48aef6f66c51c" "q-95119/selection/1fd73b79f7e3872eb8d68942dbcff463690d27a344ee4a0cc495f332fc142e50" "q-95119/selection/44734b7fd9b8fa6db618fbb8bb4edbe1ee576e76d162cea0893b4b9770639b34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95119" :question/id #uuid "c74ebdc4-1e8e-58c3-bc2d-e27edb38731f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95119" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+y)$ and $y=\\frac{1}{x},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+y),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x}), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x})+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x}))\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1-2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95119/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95088/selection/6df1d06d51b279013b208f0eec37d7e072abdaf42e2bcd92c20732d69d6228de" :answer/id #uuid "1bf3228e-0230-53d4-84f2-0a37a15d3d84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-2{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95088/selection/ef4bf3d0bfb6fc418f8352410d2be6f982c531cced7989e43daee50fdd571624" :answer/id #uuid "0c064251-3a4f-5aba-9678-eb91786b561a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{1+x{e}^{-x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95088/selection/3d7152aaf2b6a90321be8921846678d6ca89015b2a9adac168d845031f172b9f" :answer/id #uuid "19bea0db-5dd8-5ee3-af2f-2d087dfa025c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{-x}}{1+x{e}^{-x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95088/selection/2cbb7d6bd6a71ef43e1a8a75f1db7da92ec0d7154f858c542381a09d439d16d2" :answer/id #uuid "b36d55b9-593a-5ec9-87bd-77a19405c36a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95088/selection/fd9df73d546216e6fc2a62c31195c97e4b1c8dbd85e61cd430a9c41f0ca42152" :answer/id #uuid "1b35a2a4-6b46-5313-8253-a82a89030889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95088/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d616879-e133-50c3-a2d8-3aaa7795fdcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95088/selection/fd9df73d546216e6fc2a62c31195c97e4b1c8dbd85e61cd430a9c41f0ca42152" :answer-field/choices ["q-95088/selection/6df1d06d51b279013b208f0eec37d7e072abdaf42e2bcd92c20732d69d6228de" "q-95088/selection/ef4bf3d0bfb6fc418f8352410d2be6f982c531cced7989e43daee50fdd571624" "q-95088/selection/3d7152aaf2b6a90321be8921846678d6ca89015b2a9adac168d845031f172b9f" "q-95088/selection/2cbb7d6bd6a71ef43e1a8a75f1db7da92ec0d7154f858c542381a09d439d16d2" "q-95088/selection/fd9df73d546216e6fc2a62c31195c97e4b1c8dbd85e61cd430a9c41f0ca42152"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95088" :question/id #uuid "f15b5a69-260b-56fe-be10-0c6581bada1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95088" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x+y}$ and $y={e}^{-x},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}\\cdot (-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}+\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95088/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95088"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95122/selection/5f36410b1a4f572df6f09b6c18e5e86968a83b64b53560733d45be85b28df8ac" :answer/id #uuid "ff891614-1ae5-51de-9f7b-3bb0461cf582" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x(4x-3)}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95122/selection/f76f934b165838c32e114a7ee1a5d03ffaa6259457f506b891361c7f82729907" :answer/id #uuid "154a97e3-ea69-5ad4-883b-a6637f10fc5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95122/selection/a6d36966b7c23807b3e231437940f36830fcf1c0f2947d96b0b9ba2448bf002a" :answer/id #uuid "f34fb796-c3ab-5386-b050-c225cc8aa252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-1)}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95122/selection/0b68ddad013616fec31a59ebb80e5a0f517c189add38185693fe0bc1b3552c09" :answer/id #uuid "480dbbcb-0023-5725-897f-7aca3cb37afc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}(x-6)}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95122/selection/c39f543369b38148764efc4783b30ea980820a43a7d532a366c0aeccdb8dbd68" :answer/id #uuid "efb9c247-d27a-5b67-9844-9f880c46afaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x(3x+4)}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95122/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "af3b29e2-aa0e-5c69-92fb-7158535efc94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95122/selection/f76f934b165838c32e114a7ee1a5d03ffaa6259457f506b891361c7f82729907" :answer-field/choices ["q-95122/selection/5f36410b1a4f572df6f09b6c18e5e86968a83b64b53560733d45be85b28df8ac" "q-95122/selection/f76f934b165838c32e114a7ee1a5d03ffaa6259457f506b891361c7f82729907" "q-95122/selection/a6d36966b7c23807b3e231437940f36830fcf1c0f2947d96b0b9ba2448bf002a" "q-95122/selection/0b68ddad013616fec31a59ebb80e5a0f517c189add38185693fe0bc1b3552c09" "q-95122/selection/c39f543369b38148764efc4783b30ea980820a43a7d532a366c0aeccdb8dbd68"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95122" :question/id #uuid "38ad2292-5f69-5e15-93f2-ebba34819eb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95122" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x+1}$ and $y={x}^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{y}{(x+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{x+1}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{x+1}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}(x+1)-{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}{(x+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95122/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95122"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95118/selection/eb4f68ac6baff31209c2a31aa7ac15264fa064fa2916c23d6e432e2901cbd1f5" :answer/id #uuid "48514f65-6b95-53e7-a532-1e082c0875f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95118/selection/517966f855cb833fda26129e7f87ccf9be23e8b5c072b7f1419be32af7c6a3dd" :answer/id #uuid "f216995f-5b11-55f8-a47d-c91ac98e427a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95118/selection/86e6e561bd401c7be035f8fe86740c28c7521369550fefd456e5bddd2f1ac169" :answer/id #uuid "f39bb8e2-0a80-5bf7-af2f-14eb00f829ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95118/selection/a85801bff7fd487425f752ff5a3d46123eeeb317ca0a4219c25ea394b853c195" :answer/id #uuid "5c84c94b-7107-54c6-9a03-b2670eae96f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95118/selection/84733cdc913a755087638f14986e8ef495dc6ec95f52c1f4cc21e61401816647" :answer/id #uuid "4c546f7d-afab-5485-a7f8-8f30b3513e15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95118/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9049ebfd-55a2-5ac5-9841-5af2e72ddee3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95118/selection/86e6e561bd401c7be035f8fe86740c28c7521369550fefd456e5bddd2f1ac169" :answer-field/choices ["q-95118/selection/eb4f68ac6baff31209c2a31aa7ac15264fa064fa2916c23d6e432e2901cbd1f5" "q-95118/selection/517966f855cb833fda26129e7f87ccf9be23e8b5c072b7f1419be32af7c6a3dd" "q-95118/selection/86e6e561bd401c7be035f8fe86740c28c7521369550fefd456e5bddd2f1ac169" "q-95118/selection/a85801bff7fd487425f752ff5a3d46123eeeb317ca0a4219c25ea394b853c195" "q-95118/selection/84733cdc913a755087638f14986e8ef495dc6ec95f52c1f4cc21e61401816647"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95118" :question/id #uuid "3084bdd1-c471-5e59-b2f0-298bcfb435cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-95118" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+yx$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x+y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95118/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95118"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170670/selection/baa6ca39b298012acf56ab65e97de769749a98e7929716e8131b0720af762fbd" :answer/id #uuid "d805b7ed-9f1e-54e8-8d09-ad8b971836b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170670/selection/a0c2929249dc293b1eace22f4a427a1d92fe2668a10750ba379faa5660984789" :answer/id #uuid "8d4dcfd8-83bb-59c3-9e36-6ada690d5227" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170670/selection/52df362e935849c4a0dc92d3529a7321d7b61ede7eea43ae2a126a4de974d61e" :answer/id #uuid "2dee9f13-07ad-55cb-bb80-42b247ea64e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170670/selection/75ab08d61753a4faf5d663fef9091a7a8067ae64d4870a87da13ec35a0d9cf0e" :answer/id #uuid "fe3ac4e0-14c7-54ae-88bd-5ecb81e7ef51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170670/selection/6cafe5c9fe3b503c49a5718a5d78ff14c48c7567189077f6e8f33921ef0bc56c" :answer/id #uuid "5503226d-87e2-54eb-9e50-a818b226e1b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170670/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1248808b-d21c-5c85-aa37-4780ff6b93c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-170670/selection/6cafe5c9fe3b503c49a5718a5d78ff14c48c7567189077f6e8f33921ef0bc56c" :answer-field/choices ["q-170670/selection/baa6ca39b298012acf56ab65e97de769749a98e7929716e8131b0720af762fbd" "q-170670/selection/a0c2929249dc293b1eace22f4a427a1d92fe2668a10750ba379faa5660984789" "q-170670/selection/52df362e935849c4a0dc92d3529a7321d7b61ede7eea43ae2a126a4de974d61e" "q-170670/selection/75ab08d61753a4faf5d663fef9091a7a8067ae64d4870a87da13ec35a0d9cf0e" "q-170670/selection/6cafe5c9fe3b503c49a5718a5d78ff14c48c7567189077f6e8f33921ef0bc56c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-170670" :question/id #uuid "5f59a934-73d9-59a0-87fd-8e302bd7c4c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-170670" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)$ and $y={x}^{2}+1,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)}{{x}^{2}+1}=2x, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-170670/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170670"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94749/selection/ae1016ebf486017b7fb086f97805b1b6759e14a91ae2718f398d2169aef5f2d6" :answer/id #uuid "3ea85e37-bd6e-5b35-9720-b12ed016d5e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2st)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94749/selection/01b826ef0771c1fbde2271733fe079f452e65ebb3024fe18ac48a43a4138bdf8" :answer/id #uuid "cd58c6b4-f6e1-5ade-b5c2-220c88a3bb51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2st)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94749/selection/1193615316828c3aace880d176ef9eb3cdd51a71860e622c33e0bcce0eefb4af" :answer/id #uuid "eabf4728-929b-5564-a44c-ce5982993914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2st)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94749/selection/174c47b70acea7d2e1891694b11ac598a9973c8d8a4e404a1239728c7d5c5d71" :answer/id #uuid "3d15d9a9-fb69-5745-829b-9520a6549072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2st)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94749/selection/ee517ed3963c31f26de881ffdb89b867a0dffbf5bf6da66f2847eb9756273e2f" :answer/id #uuid "1b8674eb-0ae7-5d99-a017-e26a4544d687" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2st)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94749/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9703e3f-6f8f-5d59-ae26-d2f693a867dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94749/selection/ae1016ebf486017b7fb086f97805b1b6759e14a91ae2718f398d2169aef5f2d6" :answer-field/choices ["q-94749/selection/ae1016ebf486017b7fb086f97805b1b6759e14a91ae2718f398d2169aef5f2d6" "q-94749/selection/01b826ef0771c1fbde2271733fe079f452e65ebb3024fe18ac48a43a4138bdf8" "q-94749/selection/1193615316828c3aace880d176ef9eb3cdd51a71860e622c33e0bcce0eefb4af" "q-94749/selection/174c47b70acea7d2e1891694b11ac598a9973c8d8a4e404a1239728c7d5c5d71" "q-94749/selection/ee517ed3963c31f26de881ffdb89b867a0dffbf5bf6da66f2847eb9756273e2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94749" :question/id #uuid "d2bfd5e5-3484-5581-b1cc-b7e8d21b5317" :question/math-academy-id "q-94749" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=xy,$ where $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(st)$ and $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(st).$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(st), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(st).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =s\\operatorname{cos}⁡(st), \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =-s\\operatorname{sin}⁡(st).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(st))(s\\operatorname{cos}⁡(st))+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(st))(-s\\operatorname{sin}⁡(st)) \\\\  & =s{cos}^{2}⁡(st)-s{sin}^{2}⁡(st) \\\\  & =s({cos}^{2}⁡(st)-{sin}^{2}⁡(st)) \\\\  & =s\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2st).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94749/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f26d941b-b4b4-591e-b7e0-ae4bbf81e94b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94749"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170673/selection/d58424b534ef723bc627fc0f85a6978fbd36ed8e8cf1d6d9f0551e63ee61c580" :answer/id #uuid "6346cf87-c2aa-5b83-a56f-bf202aac93d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{e}^{t+s}(s-t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170673/selection/55fc359c550b71d66501129be913ee0eb6d7aba0c07758264e7373939e3113e0" :answer/id #uuid "6330caa9-b759-5795-9b4f-8e5074f0a48e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s{e}^{t+s}(t+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170673/selection/ff50ad18c296bde4658c24e11cbe5ccb2cc97bd768bd2056a226cfa19b6d2a7d" :answer/id #uuid "0dc896cc-5dd8-5e11-b2e5-84684d6fcf6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s{e}^{t+s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170673/selection/1547f1318e237051b7ea5bac09d7ae4f34d4df8407257939f01e1c569052183b" :answer/id #uuid "ceb1fd12-520c-524b-b4eb-036ae852b780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{e}^{t+s}(s+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170673/selection/4742e43d5daa413a41059d1267a283003d9c7d52f4d9591d3ca63680767d6526" :answer/id #uuid "faa41d7b-47a0-59cd-87bf-b5da7b31df9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t+s}(s+t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170673/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f844cd4b-5331-5e19-acfc-7ca2fa0e2a25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-170673/selection/1547f1318e237051b7ea5bac09d7ae4f34d4df8407257939f01e1c569052183b" :answer-field/choices ["q-170673/selection/d58424b534ef723bc627fc0f85a6978fbd36ed8e8cf1d6d9f0551e63ee61c580" "q-170673/selection/55fc359c550b71d66501129be913ee0eb6d7aba0c07758264e7373939e3113e0" "q-170673/selection/ff50ad18c296bde4658c24e11cbe5ccb2cc97bd768bd2056a226cfa19b6d2a7d" "q-170673/selection/1547f1318e237051b7ea5bac09d7ae4f34d4df8407257939f01e1c569052183b" "q-170673/selection/4742e43d5daa413a41059d1267a283003d9c7d52f4d9591d3ca63680767d6526"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-170673" :question/id #uuid "c416fc6f-25fb-59a7-937c-9a9140fd2668" :question/math-academy-id "q-170673" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=y{e}^{x},$ where $x=t+s$ and $y=ts.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =ts{e}^{t+s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{t+s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(ts{e}^{t+s})(1)+({e}^{t+s})(t) \\\\  & =t{e}^{t+s}(s+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-170673/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f26d941b-b4b4-591e-b7e0-ae4bbf81e94b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170673"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37205"] :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=2x+xy,$ where $x=s{e}^{s}$ and $y=t{e}^{s}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2+y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2+t{e}^{s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =s{e}^{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =0, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & ={e}^{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(2+t{e}^{s})(0)+(s{e}^{s})({e}^{s}) \\\\  & =s{e}^{2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-37138/selection/1b219b2502f83f3a5547453e6d60fd65fb83b5f633bd1a096eb735dcf4720a40" :answer/id #uuid "e7278562-24c4-5c8d-b137-b72cf3f29957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{s}^{6}{t}^{2}-6{s}^{2}+{t}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37138/selection/e840c8a2758c229fd9ae6ef990100a2925a16ab84861ae2fae49ce6734b4c266" :answer/id #uuid "9a5608fb-6924-5a3f-806a-c9c01ddbc750" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{s}^{6}{t}^{2}-8{s}^{3}{t}^{3}-6{s}^{2}+{t}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37138/selection/d0a21c3801c721b0070324dfbd63551682840c11e29a0dfa7c6956cf9d60589d" :answer/id #uuid "fd57f627-5212-5098-ad9a-019cfc7c020e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{s}^{3}{t}^{3}-5{s}^{2}+2{t}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37138/selection/2918998205a452219a6b31457a96246a0cad145d17f81a1de843c81d215fa258" :answer/id #uuid "d1dfbbc7-bb61-55dd-bae2-097cff955fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{s}^{3}{t}^{2}-4{s}^{3}{t}^{3}-6s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37138/selection/e343a48161e337ae719692df8c9e78b99a38d6b265bba1d42f4a5c9926d7314f" :answer/id #uuid "d9b42d5a-7a9f-523f-bfa1-7240668a08fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{s}^{5}{t}^{2}+2{s}^{3}{t}^{3}-6{s}^{2}+4{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37138/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbd427bf-cedd-5bc9-a4b3-5843d5f7aba3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37138/selection/e840c8a2758c229fd9ae6ef990100a2925a16ab84861ae2fae49ce6734b4c266" :answer-field/choices ["q-37138/selection/1b219b2502f83f3a5547453e6d60fd65fb83b5f633bd1a096eb735dcf4720a40" "q-37138/selection/e840c8a2758c229fd9ae6ef990100a2925a16ab84861ae2fae49ce6734b4c266" "q-37138/selection/d0a21c3801c721b0070324dfbd63551682840c11e29a0dfa7c6956cf9d60589d" "q-37138/selection/2918998205a452219a6b31457a96246a0cad145d17f81a1de843c81d215fa258" "q-37138/selection/e343a48161e337ae719692df8c9e78b99a38d6b265bba1d42f4a5c9926d7314f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37138" :question/id #uuid "200fb821-d757-5a5f-b920-7e5ae54a1706" :question/math-academy-id "q-37138" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-2y,$ where $x=s{t}^{2}$ and $y={s}^{3}-t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =({s}^{3}-t)^{2}={s}^{6}-2{s}^{3}t+{t}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2(s{t}^{2})({s}^{3}-t)-2=2{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-2s{t}^{3}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & ={t}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =3{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =({s}^{6}-2{s}^{3}t+{t}^{2})({t}^{2})+(2{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-2s{t}^{3}-2)(3{s}^{2}) \\\\  & ={s}^{6}{t}^{2}-2{s}^{3}{t}^{3}+{t}^{4}+6{s}^{6}{t}^{2}-6{s}^{3}{t}^{3}-6{s}^{2} \\\\  & =7{s}^{6}{t}^{2}-8{s}^{3}{t}^{3}-6{s}^{2}+{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-37138/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f26d941b-b4b4-591e-b7e0-ae4bbf81e94b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170672/selection/577275252f8ae03ee9d36fa8ea5fca590619cdf0fde5ef95f535645992049ae2" :answer/id #uuid "fefdc81b-b940-5346-8434-9bb289e3df35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡s\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170672/selection/8c5096bb1bcbe092618068f544bd1194aa82a9da7ee1a07a055211826aecb962" :answer/id #uuid "6405ecbc-222a-575f-93ac-06c22108490d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170672/selection/8ea0532204847aaa0e9ce622804d48cbc334162fb163c76087bd353bbf472edf" :answer/id #uuid "33e380ca-0c8d-5ab7-96da-a6873393bc89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170672/selection/b2f2f137fa02a8663426472001b2d58c07be80f8b2bb89aad7ab79b88403c478" :answer/id #uuid "3562ae33-e733-5f05-95c6-3021c2597542" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170672/selection/65e2e1afe64b6232c1ee52a58d998e57824bfe5f8dc6ae7a1540dfcda05c2a79" :answer/id #uuid "a85a4d02-7eb5-575e-b06e-f8e362ea6849" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170672/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "84b4ac1d-2e3f-5ec8-8f4b-c490be8bf844" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-170672/selection/577275252f8ae03ee9d36fa8ea5fca590619cdf0fde5ef95f535645992049ae2" :answer-field/choices ["q-170672/selection/577275252f8ae03ee9d36fa8ea5fca590619cdf0fde5ef95f535645992049ae2" "q-170672/selection/8c5096bb1bcbe092618068f544bd1194aa82a9da7ee1a07a055211826aecb962" "q-170672/selection/8ea0532204847aaa0e9ce622804d48cbc334162fb163c76087bd353bbf472edf" "q-170672/selection/b2f2f137fa02a8663426472001b2d58c07be80f8b2bb89aad7ab79b88403c478" "q-170672/selection/65e2e1afe64b6232c1ee52a58d998e57824bfe5f8dc6ae7a1540dfcda05c2a79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-170672" :question/id #uuid "72fe9af3-c2e0-5976-bfcc-a799e0eb9da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-170672" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=xy,$ where $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡s$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡s\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-170672/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f26d941b-b4b4-591e-b7e0-ae4bbf81e94b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170672"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170675/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "8874d854-f4f4-5d45-9b20-deeee9d70c21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170675/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ca7a1f63-e1a9-5879-b67f-fe02ad41c0fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170675/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "505e8226-e2f6-5494-b361-e53519f9a96a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170675/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "16384e39-c067-5837-90a2-fe09b9ee183a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170675/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "50874557-761c-542a-ae7e-8d956c467a96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170675/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "368fec46-9bc5-56bd-8cf9-d520b3417b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-170675/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-170675/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-170675/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-170675/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-170675/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-170675/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-170675" :question/id #uuid "c0285d27-5a91-54ee-863f-f3912e6a5c27" :question/math-academy-id "q-170675" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{y+z}{x},$ where $x=s+t,$ $y={s}^{2}$ and $z={t}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{{c}_{1}{s}^{2}+{c}_{2}st+{c}_{3}{t}^{2}}{(s+t)^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the value of ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{y+z}{{x}^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}+{t}^{2}}{(s+t)^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{s+t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{1}{s+t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =0, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}+{t}^{2}}{(s+t)^{2}}\\cdot (1)+\\frac{1}{s+t}\\cdot 0+\\frac{1}{s+t}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =\\frac{-({s}^{2}+{t}^{2})+2t(s+t)}{(s+t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}+2ts-{s}^{2}}{(s+t)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${c}_{1}=-1,$ ${c}_{2}=2$ and ${c}_{3}=1,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}=-1+2+1=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-170675/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170675"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37132/selection/a26964b671342b5e202be5d90e3ce34f776eced13e609602a880ab3951144444" :answer/id #uuid "20837b1a-9dcd-5a17-8c18-12d104c9b776" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{s}^{4}t-5{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37132/selection/69b898bff0a5c4b5b9f181b30de0129c65e6ac47082288d935548ddfcfd2ce6a" :answer/id #uuid "907b5116-aa60-5e10-bc1d-fb0501546074" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{s}^{4}{t}^{2}+10{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37132/selection/48cc945a401dbac410e920cd009cec921fe4111a3e329ef2c229dd065dc82e4f" :answer/id #uuid "a0c032c6-47b9-5602-950c-80e4e8d61d5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{s}^{2}{t}^{4}-20s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37132/selection/b4aa8db13f865968ea2db610b40b51b1e1df006786b56fffcc01dbc1da9b61a2" :answer/id #uuid "34bf89e2-3d4d-511e-8026-987cf8dc253d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-20{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37132/selection/7e8ce79dcefa561496843e5cc8d2a369ec4bcea5d3bd6f5eaf34df762c241102" :answer/id #uuid "b856053d-fde3-5a92-805a-e870329571da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{s}^{2}{t}^{4}-15s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37132/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "87dc0339-4fc6-5b24-bbeb-393044063084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37132/selection/b4aa8db13f865968ea2db610b40b51b1e1df006786b56fffcc01dbc1da9b61a2" :answer-field/choices ["q-37132/selection/a26964b671342b5e202be5d90e3ce34f776eced13e609602a880ab3951144444" "q-37132/selection/69b898bff0a5c4b5b9f181b30de0129c65e6ac47082288d935548ddfcfd2ce6a" "q-37132/selection/48cc945a401dbac410e920cd009cec921fe4111a3e329ef2c229dd065dc82e4f" "q-37132/selection/b4aa8db13f865968ea2db610b40b51b1e1df006786b56fffcc01dbc1da9b61a2" "q-37132/selection/7e8ce79dcefa561496843e5cc8d2a369ec4bcea5d3bd6f5eaf34df762c241102"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37132" :question/id #uuid "39a13e63-80c2-510a-a176-983055df39bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-37132" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y-5yz,$ where $x=st,$ $y={s}^{3}$ and $z=s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}-5z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-5y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(st)({s}^{3})=2{s}^{4}t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(st)^{2}-5(s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)={s}^{2}{t}^{2}-5s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =-5{s}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =t, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =3{s}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(2{s}^{4}t)\\cdot t+({s}^{2}{t}^{2}-5s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 3{s}^{2}+(-5{s}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =2{s}^{4}{t}^{2}+3{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-15{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =5{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-20{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-37132/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37132"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94816/selection/d4c03f7656093028aa8072c294e8d964cd4395ab86ff18a154dd25a5260ca684" :answer/id #uuid "5f471692-18b5-5e28-80d9-f3cafbcddd2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}-{s}^{2}}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94816/selection/f51dcd52057dd9e3729f5eea5fe3726c5c20cc9c725806f682703e55bec8fd31" :answer/id #uuid "f3115d56-c996-52a9-9fa4-83a40f1f3531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{st+1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94816/selection/73e0e88efed2dcf858516e0c0d5fd472adc0282fbbb21ce4c1831ab908138765" :answer/id #uuid "af0ddd68-d47f-57cc-b0eb-868da8ab44fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+2{s}^{2})}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94816/selection/60a47a6c4825b9a545d3b198cb87495b300f2539bcf6852a255d765ee5f6283f" :answer/id #uuid "a631c9b1-f15a-567c-8779-26da12a59286" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "st({s}^{2}{t}^{2}+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94816/selection/71f1164553a1b1edee105e4962c8f1f5c8f561f2cdca95bd17a49159c560a78c" :answer/id #uuid "371e683f-4245-5dc5-bc94-f0b1e611b893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+{t}^{2}}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94816/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e52e23f4-47d9-5bf1-b5e3-59f36d43abb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94816/selection/73e0e88efed2dcf858516e0c0d5fd472adc0282fbbb21ce4c1831ab908138765" :answer-field/choices ["q-94816/selection/d4c03f7656093028aa8072c294e8d964cd4395ab86ff18a154dd25a5260ca684" "q-94816/selection/f51dcd52057dd9e3729f5eea5fe3726c5c20cc9c725806f682703e55bec8fd31" "q-94816/selection/73e0e88efed2dcf858516e0c0d5fd472adc0282fbbb21ce4c1831ab908138765" "q-94816/selection/60a47a6c4825b9a545d3b198cb87495b300f2539bcf6852a255d765ee5f6283f" "q-94816/selection/71f1164553a1b1edee105e4962c8f1f5c8f561f2cdca95bd17a49159c560a78c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94816" :question/id #uuid "f54cad8f-6f81-5bf1-9373-fb4d7af3562f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94816" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{e}^{y}+4z,$ where $x=t{s}^{2},$ $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+{s}^{2})$ and $z={s}^{2}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2{e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{t{s}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+{s}^{2})}=-2({t}^{2}+{s}^{2}), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2ts, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =\\frac{2s}{{t}^{2}+{s}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(\\frac{1}{t{s}^{2}})\\cdot 2ts+(-2({t}^{2}+{s}^{2}))\\cdot (\\frac{2s}{{t}^{2}+{s}^{2}})+(4)\\cdot 2s \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-4s+8s \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}+4s \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+2{s}^{2})}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94816/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94816"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94815/selection/95031683ed34cdd76dcf5d71e06a5335b34a86e7009565b63f0d3d37c754f7e5" :answer/id #uuid "30c76fc8-8ac2-55a8-a278-c2cfa5863a33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(st+s-t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94815/selection/2640fd689a1a0b36a619e67cfade9b7e1858991596d50b9dbe693342edea0249" :answer/id #uuid "8bf30693-4866-5a63-937c-d6ea81fe9c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(5s-t+s{t}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94815/selection/64f7d2a163df62caa53e4c00d331e1bcfd5319632feaf3c10585a2bf5f990b28" :answer/id #uuid "24564973-e0da-5365-a4d4-47755aa07a0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s(t+s)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94815/selection/a453431c89d434c2928fa83a55776341472a3885bcd66a074c8691a3b12c473e" :answer/id #uuid "74e37fcd-b4b0-5ec1-8ff0-734da93392fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t(5-s)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94815/selection/12912b3932e3b4527d434ca53870a0306624a12f027a1eeeb4117971a71d117c" :answer/id #uuid "a5809ec2-a496-5b6b-9be7-47681ddd6d88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3s-5t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94815/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d38d470-41a5-5d18-9c6d-0f46200ccd38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94815/selection/2640fd689a1a0b36a619e67cfade9b7e1858991596d50b9dbe693342edea0249" :answer-field/choices ["q-94815/selection/95031683ed34cdd76dcf5d71e06a5335b34a86e7009565b63f0d3d37c754f7e5" "q-94815/selection/2640fd689a1a0b36a619e67cfade9b7e1858991596d50b9dbe693342edea0249" "q-94815/selection/64f7d2a163df62caa53e4c00d331e1bcfd5319632feaf3c10585a2bf5f990b28" "q-94815/selection/a453431c89d434c2928fa83a55776341472a3885bcd66a074c8691a3b12c473e" "q-94815/selection/12912b3932e3b4527d434ca53870a0306624a12f027a1eeeb4117971a71d117c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94815" :question/id #uuid "6fdd6111-6c8f-562a-b585-e0b803a94563" :question/math-academy-id "q-94815" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2},$ where $x=t+2s,$ $y=3t-s$ and $z=st.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(t+2s)=2t+4s, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2(3t-s)=6t-2s, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =2st.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(2t+4s)\\cdot 2+(6t-2s)\\cdot (-1)+(2st)\\cdot t \\\\  & =4t+8s-6t+2s+2s{t}^{2} \\\\  & =10s-2t+2s{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2(5s-t+s{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94815/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94815"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94812/selection/9de5d9285ee2568197e928ce7c825353e5c0ddf20104094703a95945e35d4d99" :answer/id #uuid "46ae10af-1def-5371-9dcb-55bc31c10af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t(s+1){e}^{t+s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94812/selection/6f345de141c6e3de8cb6392005c0af6583b160e7834c22b07c9126364d8d8a10" :answer/id #uuid "bf59e1e7-0b31-57f2-88b3-f63cf40d53b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2s(t+1){e}^{t+s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94812/selection/8636565bc75753270ab8a9c5799a30810788fb7b7f99c0ba890e23d0fe49de1c" :answer/id #uuid "dd78109e-8abd-5f23-940a-2c93f303b365" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t(s-1){e}^{t+s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94812/selection/1abd41f4660baca6219cc44e625d6602177ea259f2e2f1ac19fb63fae6731b0f" :answer/id #uuid "fa889f70-284b-55c3-988d-184cc294d6e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(t-s){e}^{t+s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94812/selection/13b562e39f570e80d236ad5e87b98bfdb4547e1b14003d9028f45cb4eddfcbb5" :answer/id #uuid "0d89b8cf-6caf-5298-9440-92429d6ddf4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(t+s){e}^{t+s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94812/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b498291b-53fd-50bf-af45-63cad4c51b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94812/selection/6f345de141c6e3de8cb6392005c0af6583b160e7834c22b07c9126364d8d8a10" :answer-field/choices ["q-94812/selection/9de5d9285ee2568197e928ce7c825353e5c0ddf20104094703a95945e35d4d99" "q-94812/selection/6f345de141c6e3de8cb6392005c0af6583b160e7834c22b07c9126364d8d8a10" "q-94812/selection/8636565bc75753270ab8a9c5799a30810788fb7b7f99c0ba890e23d0fe49de1c" "q-94812/selection/1abd41f4660baca6219cc44e625d6602177ea259f2e2f1ac19fb63fae6731b0f" "q-94812/selection/13b562e39f570e80d236ad5e87b98bfdb4547e1b14003d9028f45cb4eddfcbb5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94812" :question/id #uuid "c71a1fc7-14f8-5f45-8aa5-6faf468933ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-94812" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=xyz,$ where $x=2,$ $y=s{e}^{t}$ and $z=t{e}^{s}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=yz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=xz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =ts{e}^{t+s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2t{e}^{s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =2s{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =0, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =s{e}^{t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & ={e}^{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =(ts{e}^{t+s})\\cdot 0+(2t{e}^{s})\\cdot s{e}^{t}+(2s{e}^{t})\\cdot {e}^{s} \\\\  & =2ts{e}^{t+s}+2s{e}^{t+s} \\\\  & =2s(t+1){e}^{t+s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94812/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8256"] :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\cos(xy), x=t,$ and $y=e^t,$ compute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x = x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}t} \n= \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t}), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =[-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t})]\\cdot 1+[-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t})]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t})-t{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =-(1+t){e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8257"] :question/problem "If $f(x,y) = 2\\sqrt{x+y}$ and $y=\\cos x,$ compute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y = y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+y}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8258"] :question/problem "Let $f(x,y) = x^2 + y^2,$ where $x = s\\cos{t}$ and $y = t\\sin{s}.$ Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y = y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t} = \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial x}{\\partial t} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2s\\operatorname{cos}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =-s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(2s\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(-s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡s) \\\\  & =-2{s}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t{sin}^{2}⁡s \\\\  & =2t{sin}^{2}⁡s-2{s}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =2t{sin}^{2}⁡s-{s}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the identity $\\sin 2t = 2\\sin t\\cos t$ in the above simplification." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8259"] :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z) = e^{xy + z},$ where $x = s + t,$ $y = s-t$ and $z = -s^2.$ Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t), y = y(s,t)$ and $z = z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t} = \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial x}{\\partial t} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial y}{\\partial t} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x, y$ and $z\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{xy+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={e}^{xy+z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(s-t){e}^{(s+t)(s-t)-{s}^{2}}=(s-t){e}^{-{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(s+t){e}^{(s+t)(s-t)-{s}^{2}}=(s+t){e}^{-{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & ={e}^{(s+t)(s-t)-{s}^{2}}={e}^{-{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =(s-t){e}^{-{t}^{2}}\\cdot 1+(s+t){e}^{-{t}^{2}}\\cdot (-1)+{e}^{-{t}^{2}}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =(s-t-s-t){e}^{-{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{-{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
